From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:47:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 382/384] dt-bindings: input: gpio-matrix-keypad: add
 held-poll-interval

In row interrupt mode, the matrix drives every column between scans, so
a pressed key holds its row asserted. A second key pressed in that row
changes nothing on the row line and raises no interrupt. Keyboards put
modifiers in rows with letters, so the second key is lost.

Add an optional interval at which the matrix keeps being scanned while
any key is held. Row interrupts take over again once all keys are
released.

Not yet run on hardware.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml    | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
index a9fab526b..9181ad3a0 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/gpio-matrix-keypad.yaml
@@ -76,6 +76,15 @@ properties:
       interval instead of requesting interrupts for the row GPIOs. Polling
       cannot wake a suspended system.
 
+  held-poll-interval:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    minimum: 1
+    description:
+      With row interrupts, keep scanning the matrix at this interval in
+      milliseconds while any key is held, and return to row interrupts once
+      all keys are released. A held key keeps its row asserted, so a second
+      key in the same row raises no row interrupt and is otherwise missed.
+
   drive-inactive-cols:
     type: boolean
     description:
